<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Hustlers</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;July 1964 and Strategic Air Command strikes the People's Republic of China's (PRC) nuclear weapons development program.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You are Commander, 64th Bombardment Squadron (Medium) of the 43rd Bombardment Wing, Strategic Air Command (SAC) based at Carswell, AFB, Texas. Wing Operations has advised that your squadron has been stood down from Alert status and you are to immediately fly to SAC HQ at Offut AFB by Lockheed C-140 Jetstar executive transport.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In March 1964 senior members of the American national security apparatus met to discuss nuclear issues and one item on the agenda was the growing threat of the Communist Chinese nuclear weapons program. Imagery from the Corona/Discoverer family of satellites had disclosed increasing nuclear weapons-related infrastructure being built at Lop Nur in western China and the idea of "taking out" the program using a preemptive, precision nuclear strike was proposed. In the event, the proposal was rejected but what if approval had been given?&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Analysis has determined that a strike by ICBM is impractical and dangerous. The Soviets could not be certain that the missiles were not aimed at them and would probably launch a counter-strike when the incoming missiles were detected. SLBMs from the Eastern Indian Ocean might minimize the chance of an immediate Soviet nuclear response but the best bet for success is a surgical strike by the Strategic Air Command. For SAC, the bomber of choice for this operations would be the B-58A Hustler. Now satellite photographs have revealed what has been assessed as the shot tower along with command and scientific infrastructure in proximity to the production site. It is clear that a live nuclear test is months and perhaps only weeks away.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;You have been selected to plan and execute OPERATION QUIET CONCERT, a preemptive nuclear attack on China's nuclear weapons program. Mission assets, including some of your B-58A bombers have be sent to the British Indian Ocean territory of Diego Garcia from which you will launch the raid.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Chinese nuclear weapon production facilities and the test site are at the limits of the B-58s operational range&amp;nbsp;and a high-altitude ingress and attack profile&amp;nbsp;probably offer the greatest chance of mission success. The reactors and fissile processing plants at Lop Nur are defended but isolated. Every effort must be made to minimize civilian casualties and incidental damage to non-weapon&amp;nbsp; related infrastructure. Extensive intelligence briefings are included but there is much that is unknown. You're on your own for mission planning but the Pentagon has limited the strike assets available. They want you to use no more than two strike aircraft (one of which is a spare) and a maximum of ten weapons, eight of which will be the 340-KT B.61 with two 9-MT B.53 bombs. There are also restrictions on what nations are available for over-flights and where air to air refuelling may be conducted. Four Hustlers have been sent to Diego Garcia so you have reserve planes. If you can make the case for the 1-MT B.43 in lue of the&amp;nbsp;lower-yield B.61s they will be reluctantly allocated to the mission.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario Author's Notes.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;While the operation code name is fictional, the discussions within the National Security community to postpone a Communist Chinese atomic bomb by a limited, preemptive nuclear attack were almost certainly&amp;nbsp;not. However as the actual documentation is still classified, we are free to use CMANO to game out this strike.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;The political consequences of a preemptive, surprise nuclear attack on the People's Republic of China are incalculable. Perhaps it would give aspiring nuclear powers like India and Pakistan reason to dampen their atomic ambitions or spur a new global arms race, wrecking any prospects for some sort of international non-proliferation regime. Or the USSR might have been emboldened to strike at Israel's Dimona nuclear facility, then under development with French assistance given the precedent established by the United States. Almost certainly the US would have come under intense diplomatic attack in the United Nations and the Third World while it is entirely possible that NATO nations would make every effort to distance themselves from America's actions. On the other hand, such an attack would be most welcome in certain political quarters at home and while the anti-nuclear lobby and national peace movements would have been appalled, there is also a chance that domestic political fallout might have been minimal.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Of course at this time the United States was becoming increasingly involved in Vietnam and how the fallout from an unprovoked nuclear strike on the PRC,&amp;nbsp; North Vietnam's communist neighbour and patron can only be conjectured. So it is perhaps a good thing that the national security wonks determined that a Chinese bomb was probably not an existential threat to America that required immediate&amp;nbsp;termination with extreme prejudice.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The Player has two special actions to increase the available strike assets and/or use more powerful weapons with the commiserate threat of increasing collateral damage. The more damage done to PRC non-nuclear infrastructure, including defence facilities, the greater the number of Victory Points that are subtracted from the Player total. Your mission is to destroy the ability of the PRC to manufacture and test nuclear weapons, minimizing your losses and those of Chinese not involved in the weapons program.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The scenario is designed to place a premium on Player mission planning and while the&amp;nbsp;attack&amp;nbsp;itself should be&amp;nbsp;relatively straitforward, the long distance engress and egress to near the limits of your aircraft's&amp;nbsp;endurance envelope and the necessity to employ multiple tanker sorties complicates the process. During testing, it&amp;nbsp;proved possible to completely automate the air refueling missions so despite the many claims from some quarters that this capability is "broken", the AAR model in current CMANO version can successfully recreate complex tanker missions. The RAF tanker scheme for the May 1982 BLACK BUCK raids on Port Stanley Airport was used a a model for tanker sorties during testing but no specific guidence is offered and it's up to the Player to solve this problem on their own.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;There are a number of over flight restrictions that will cost heavily in Victory Points if they are triggered. These&amp;nbsp;represent&amp;nbsp;an attempt to mitigate&amp;nbsp;the political backlash that can be expected should QUIET CONCERT succeed. Read the CINCSAC briefing carefully and ensure that none of the airspace prohibitions or targeting&amp;nbsp;violations are triggered. Losses to the strike force are also intolerable and incure major penalties and may even result in Player defeat on points.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Enjoy.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Christopher Comars aka Randomizer&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
